  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One distribution, two origins",
      "items": [
        "The Router is created empty, then routed once the bucket exists",
        "/uploads/* is the more specific route, so it beats the app's default /*",
        "Uploads are same-origin: no second domain, no CORS on reads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Two entry points, one rulebook",
      "items": [
        "Public pages call the domain services in-process — no network hop",
        "The backoffice calls the Hono API server-to-server; the browser never holds a token",
        "Both land on the same @awsug/core services, so rules cannot drift"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Identity is Cognito, authorisation is the database",
      "items": [
        "Hosted UI with authorization-code + PKCE; the exchange happens server-side",
        "The API verifies with aws-jwt-verify using tokenUse 'id' — it needs the email claim",
        "A verified token still needs a matching users row, or it is a 403"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The crossing that pays for the rest",
      "items": [
        "Aurora is the only thing inside the VPC; both Lambdas stay outside it",
        "They reach it over the Data API's HTTPS endpoint — so no NAT Gateway, ~$43/month saved",
        "Auto-pause is incompatible with RDS Proxy, which is the second reason for the Data API"
      ]
    }
  ]
